WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.913
The answer to check one: no.

2
00:00:01.913 --> 00:00:05.351
Only an enabled log to the
platform workspace counts.

3
00:00:05.351 --> 00:00:06.213
Scene two.

4
00:00:06.213 --> 00:00:10.941
Steps 3 to 5 can't be proved complete
without a list of what's exposed,

5
00:00:10.941 --> 00:00:15.153
and the portal is public in many
places: a Front Door profile,

6
00:00:15.153 --> 00:00:20.138
the gateway's address, a jump box, a
load balancer, two web apps and a vault.

7
00:00:20.138 --> 00:00:24.866
The kit joins the guide's Resource
Graph queries, built from Microsoft

8
00:00:24.866 --> 00:00:29.350
Learn's starter sample, into one
register, with an owner on every row.

9
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.837
The jump box's address has no owner.

10
00:00:31.837 --> 00:00:36.625
A week later a new address appears,
with no owner either, and an orphan

11
00:00:36.625 --> 00:00:42.070
address is gone, with a reminder to remove
any DNS record still pointing at it.
